The previous implementation fetched every item in a single `repository.loadMany(ids)` call; the rewrite issues `repository.load(id)` once per loop iteration, so round-trips now scale with the size of `ids` even though the batch API still exists. Iterate the batch result and filter instead:

    var results = ResultListFactory.create();
    for (var item : repository.loadMany(ids)) {
      if (item.active() && item.owner() != null && item.owner().enabled()) {
        results.add(item);
      }
    }
    return results;

