findings.body:
Each iteration awaits repository.load(id) individually, replacing the single batched repository.loadMany(ids) call the function used before. Round-trips now scale with ids.length, and the serial await pays each round-trip's latency in sequence. If loadMany cannot express the new filtering, restructure to a batch plus filter:

  const items = await repository.loadMany(ids);
  return items.filter((item) => item.active && item.owner && item.owner.enabled);

or at least fan out concurrently with Promise.all(ids.map((id) => repository.load(id))).

